DFlash: feed generated tokens to the penalizers (SGLang nightly-cu134-20260909-708f51e, speculative/spec_utils.py).

ScheduleBatch.prepare_for_decode returns before cumulate_penalty_output_tokens() for speculative batches. EAGLE
calls it itself (feeding the last token a step); DFlash never did, so with ./start-dflash.sh presence_penalty,
frequency_penalty and repetition_penalty never saw a generated token and had no effect: greedy replies with
presence_penalty 0 and 1.5 were byte-identical (with ./start.sh they differ). This feeds, at each DFlash decode
prep, every output token a request gained since its previous step (up to a block), one position at a time:
presence/repetition (set-based) pad shorter requests with their last token (idempotent), frequency/min_new_tokens
(count-based) add only real tokens. Under overlap scheduling the newest tokens arrive a step later, as for EAGLE.
Verified: greedy presence_penalty 0 vs 1.5 now differ under DFlash, and the default equals an explicit 1.5.

